The [[Trax Tube]] was a [[Mid Rim Territories]] [[hyperspace route]]<ref name="BMF 43" /> that was also part of [[the Slice]] region of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Slice" /> It had one terminus at<ref name="GM" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="LivingForce" /> [[Randon]] which acted as a junction onto<ref name="GM" /> the [[Ootmian Pabol]],<ref name="LivingForce" /> the [[Pabol Sleheyron]], and the [[Randon Run]].<ref name="Randon" /> The Trax Tube then traveled down through the astronomical objects [[Deysum system|Deysum]] and [[Uogo'cor system|Uogo'cor]]<ref name="TFABG" /> then the [[Typhonic Nebula]] and<ref name="GM" /> the planets<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref><ref name="CR4">[[Crimson Reign 4|''Crimson Reign'' 4]]</ref> [[Grange]] and [[Varnak]].<ref name="GM" />

At the planet<ref name="Heir" /> [[Nanth'ri]]<ref name="GM" /> in the [[Nanth'ri system]]<ref name="Heir" /> there was another junction<ref name="GM" /> on to the [[Nanth'ri Trade Route]]<ref name="Heir" /> after which the Trax Tube linked to the celestial body [[Nixor system|Nixor]]<ref name="TFABG" /> before terminating at the astronomical object [[Daalang]].<ref name="GM" /> Daalang was also part of the [[Gamor Run]] and was connected to<ref name="GM" /> the planet<ref name="UCB">''[[Star Wars: The Ultimate Cookbook]]''</ref> [[Circumtore]] and the astronomical object [[Demiloch]] by two other routes. On the [[Standard Galactic Grid]], the Trax Tube passed through squares Q-10, Q-11, and Q-12.<ref name="GM" />

==Behind the scenes==
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the Trax Tube was first pictured in "Sectors of the Galaxy," an article in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 18|eighteenth]] issue of the ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine,<ref name="BMF18">{{BuildFalconCite|18|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> which was published around [[May 6]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate18">{{BuildFalconDates|18}}</ref> It was then identified in "Kashyyyk's Fight for Freedom," an article in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 43|forty-third]] issue of the same magazine<ref name="BMF 43" /> released around [[October 28]], 2015.<ref name="BMFdate43">{{BuildFalconDates|43}}</ref>

